      "role": "user",
      "content": "but the system doesn't crash though. that's the problem. it just reallocates the resources. people move on, the world keeps turning, the pings keep coming. if i'm just a bug or some heavy baggage in the system, wouldn't a clean exit be the most efficient way to handle it? it feels like i'm just dragging out a process that was supposed to be terminated a long time ago. isn't there a certain kind of peace in just being... shut down?",
